    {"text": "objects a story flag hides, not placed: var_0 at (46, 52) (flag 408); doctor at (47, 4) (flag 443); gingam at (46, 3) (flag 442); gingam at (46, 4) (flag 442); bigman at (58, 20) (flag 426); middleman2 at (46, 35) (flag 532); clown at (55, 33) (flag 531); clown at (15, 18) (flag 531); clown at (36, 16) (flag 598); bigman at (45, 17) (flag 425)", "source": "decomp"},
    {"text": "38 walkable tiles not connected to (46, 62) are unknown: they are other components of the game map (one map, one connected component)", "source": "generator"},
    {"text": "Tile (x, y) is world (128 + x, 736 + y) of pokediamond's matrix 0. The image-traced file this replaces had 12 px rows for 16 px columns, so its rows do not map one to one onto these: its row 10 is row 15 here, its row 30 row 40 and its rows 44..46 rows 61..63.", "source": "decomp comparison, 2026-10-31"},
    {"text": "Console-verified: the TV station door row (15), the School and Center door row (40), and the street from the steps to the north exit along columns 46..47, open the whole way. The console's measurements put the doors one column west of the image trace (lamps at (43, 53) and (49, 53), 'north from (50, 39)' ending in front of the Center at column 52 here).", "source": "console (lab B)"},
    {"text": "To re-verify: the Pokemon Center door is 12 tiles east of the School doorway here (52 against 40), 11 on the console; the lamps' row stops (west at the house, east at the house) fit the decomp's row 52, one above the lamps on 53.", "source": "console (lab B) vs decomp"},
    {"text": "The story's people (the clowns, the Poketch president) are hidden behind flags in the decomp and are placed here from the console, on the decomp's tiles for them.", "source": "console (lab B)"},
    {"text": "Diamond and Platinum differ around the Global Trade Station (x 15..26, y 35..44): Diamond's smaller building leaves an enclosed pocket north of it, kept unknown here; BDSP's Global Wonder Station stands there.", "source": "pret/pokediamond vs pret/pokeplatinum"},
    {"text": "Exits: south (40..49, 62..63) through the neck (45..47, 61) to Route 202; north (42..55, 0) to Route 204 South (its east strip, (54..55, 0), is a dead end); east rows 21..24 to Route 203; west (0, 22..23) are warp tiles into the Route 218 gatehouse.", "source": "decomp, read by hand"}
